.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH octosnap 1  OctoSnap 
.SH NAME
octosnap \- OctoSnap command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBoctosnap\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Screenshot, annotation and screen\-recording tool for GNOME on Wayland.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
octosnap\-capture(1)
Take a screenshot
.TP
octosnap\-record(1)
Record a GIF of a rectangle for a fixed time, in this process rather than the app
.TP
octosnap\-stop\-recording(1)
Stop the recording in progress. Does nothing when nothing is recording
.TP
octosnap\-open(1)
Open a .octosnap project for editing
.TP
octosnap\-settings(1)
Open the settings window
.TP
octosnap\-copy\-last(1)
Put the most recent capture back on the clipboard
.TP
octosnap\-save\-last(1)
Write the most recent capture to the export location
.TP
octosnap\-pin(1)
Pin an image to the screen
.TP
octosnap\-annotate(1)
Open an image, or a .octosnap project, in the annotation editor
.TP
octosnap\-open\-from\-clipboard(1)
Open the clipboard\*(Aqs image in the annotation editor
.TP
octosnap\-desktop\-icons(1)
Hide, show or toggle the desktop icons
.TP
octosnap\-add\-overlay(1)
Add an image file to the Quick Access Overlay as a card
.TP
octosnap\-text(1)
Recognise the text in an image and copy it
.TP
octosnap\-history(1)
Open the capture history
.TP
octosnap\-restore(1)
Bring back the most recently closed card
.TP
octosnap\-ping(1)
Check that the app answers, starting it if it is not running
.TP
octosnap\-shell\-version(1)
Report the shell extension\*(Aqs version and protocol
.TP
octosnap\-monitors(1)
Print the monitor layout as the extension sees it, in logical coordinates
.TP
octosnap\-status(1)
Report on the app and the shell extension at once
